    <!-- Column 4 Text -->
    <div slot="col-4-text">
      <p>
        Remembering, when just a wee lassie <br />
        The Term fun day in Kirrie Square <br />
        Spending a ha’penny at the Muckley <br />
        At the stalls all erected there.
      </p>

      <p>
        Walking in wi’ my Gran and Grandy <br />
        To me it was a real holiday <br />
        Toddling hame tired but happy <br />
        Clutching toys at the close of day.
      </p>

      <p>
        Gone now are those simple joys <br />
        That filled 0ur hearts with delight <br />
        To see a field of horses now <br />
        And men ploughing – a lovely sight.
      </p>

      <p>
        Fields of stooks drying in the sunshine <br />
        High stacks built up in farm yards <br />
        Are some things you no longer see now <br />
        Yet was real fodder to the Bard.
      </p>

      <p>
        Life no doubt is much easier now <br />
        The old Term dates met their fate <br />
        But I’m glad that I was born back then <br />
        Such Happy Memories they still create.
      </p>
    </div>

